<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74726" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρ-ᾱσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seeing, the act of sight,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Demad.
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1174a14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				123
			</span></i>, etc. ; distd. as the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέργεια</span> or <i>act</i> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψις</span> (the sense or faculty), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>de An.</u>
				426a13
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				428a7
			</span></i>; but, <i>power of sight</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1141
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thrace</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> pl., <i>eyes,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ὁ. ἐκκόπτειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					2.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				8.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.88d
			</span></i> : metaph., as title of the daughter-goddess of the Sun,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρασιν αὑτοῦ</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ Ἡλίου</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				56.56
			</span></i> (Canopus, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a vision,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jl.</u>
				2.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				2.17
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>appearance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅμοιος ὁράσει λίθῳ ἰάσπιδι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Apoc.</u>
					4.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ μεταμορφούμενος ἐν ταῖς ὁράσεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLeid.W.</u>
					13.36
				</span></i>
			.</div>
